# Verification

The single most important practice for quality output: **always verify your work.**

## After Every Change

1. **Run lints** — use ReadLints on every file you edited
2. **Fix what you broke** — if lints were introduced by your changes, fix them immediately
3. **Check types** — run `bun run build` if the change touches types, exports, or cross-file references
4. **Test in browser** — for UI changes, use the browser-use subagent to visually verify the result

## Before Considering a Task Done

- Re-read the changed files to confirm correctness
- Verify imports resolve (no missing modules)
- Confirm no unused variables or imports were left behind
- If you modified a server action or API route, trace the data flow end-to-end

## When Things Go Wrong

- If a fix attempt makes things worse, **stop and re-plan** — switch to Plan mode
- Never stack fix-on-fix more than twice — scrap and implement the clean solution
- After a mediocre fix: "Knowing everything you know now, scrap this and implement the elegant solution"

## Feedback Loops by Domain

| Domain         | Verification Method                                      |
| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| UI components  | Browser subagent — navigate and visually inspect         |
| API routes     | Trace request → handler → database → response           |
| Server actions | Check Supabase query, error handling, return types       |
| Styling        | Browser subagent — check responsive, dark mode           |
| Types          | `bun run build` to catch type errors                     |
| Lint           | ReadLints on all edited files                            |
